% Generate `web/src/UpdateBanner.jsx`: the lower-left "update ready" card for the packaged
% Electron shell. It appears only after electron-updater has downloaded a newer build (see
% desktop/main.js `initAutoUpdate`); clicking "Restart & update" tells the main process to
% `quitAndInstall()`. In a browser or in dev there is no preload bridge / no updater, so
% `window.openNolan.update` is absent (or its handlers reject) and the banner stays hidden.
% Imports `useEffect, useState` from 'react'. No inline styles — the `update-toast*` class
% names below are the contract with web/src/styles.css.

Default-export `UpdateBanner()` (no props).

State: `version` — `undefined` means none/unknown so the banner is hidden, a string means an
update is staged (may be `''` when the staged version is unknown); `installing` — boolean.

Mount effect (runs once): read `const u = window.openNolan?.update`; if absent, do nothing.
Otherwise (a) re-hydrate across renderer reloads by calling `u.getState?.()`, and on a truthy
result `setVersion(s.version || '')` (swallow rejects); (b) subscribe to live download pushes
via `u.onDownloaded?.(info => setVersion((info && info.version) || ''))` — `onDownloaded`
returns its own unsubscribe, which is returned as this effect's cleanup.

While `version === undefined`, render `null`.

`install()` (async): set `installing` true, then `await window.openNolan.update.install()`; if
it throws, reset `installing` to false (on success the app quits to install, so no reset).

Render an `update-toast` div (`role="status"`) containing:
- an `update-toast-body` with an `update-toast-title` "Update ready" and an `update-toast-sub`
  reading `Version {version} will install on restart.` when `version` is truthy, else
  `A new version will install on restart.`
- an `update-toast-btn` button (onClick `install`, disabled while `installing`) labelled
  "Restarting…" while installing, else "Restart & update".
- an `update-toast-x` dismiss button (aria-label "Dismiss", glyph ×) that re-hides the banner
  by setting `version` back to `undefined`.
